<title>UK: UK government confirms beef statement due Monday.</title>
<headline>UK government confirms beef statement due Monday.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British government confirmed that Agriculture Minister Douglas Hogg would make a statement to parliament later on Monday on mad cow disease and the export ban on British beef.</p>
<p>Hogg's statement will follow one at 1530 GMT by Prime Minister John Major, who will report back on his weekend visit to Dublin for a European Union summit, an aide to Major said.</p>
<p>Hogg is widely expected to announce plans for a selective slaughter of a further 100,000 cattle in a bid to bring forward the lifting of the European Union export ban.</p>
</text>
